/**
 * Coastlines for the map, in longitude and latitude.
 *
 * Natural Earth 1:50m for the country plates and 1:110m land for the world
 * overview, via world-atlas, simplified with Ramer–Douglas–Peucker to the point
 * where a country still reads as itself and no further. Hand-drawing these was
 * tried first and Italy did not look like Italy.
 *
 * Server-side only. The map renders to SVG on the server, so what crosses the
 * wire is the path data for the one view being looked at, not this whole file.
 *
 * Rings are exterior only — a lake inside a country is not worth the bytes at
 * this scale — and each country keeps at most its twelve largest, which drops
 * the islands that would otherwise be a single pixel of noise.
 */

/** A closed ring of [longitude, latitude] pairs. */
